name measuring-hate-speech-annotations
# The set's file is Parquet; it is written out beside it as a table (extracted/): the first row the columns' own
# names, every value as the file holds it.
# The set's card (README.md): "39,565 comments annotated by 7,912 annotators, for 135,556 combined rows", and
# ("Key dataset columns"):
#   comment_id - unique ID for each comment          annotator_id - unique ID for each annotator
#   text - lightly processed text of a social media post
#   hate_speech_score - continuous hate speech measure
#   sentiment, respect, insult, humiliate, status, dehumanize, violence, genocide, attack_defend, hatespeech -
#     ordinal label that is combined into the continuous score
#   annotator_severity - annotator's estimated survey interpretation bias
# The recipe's reading, not the card's words: a row is one annotator's reading of one comment. What the annotator
# answered of the comment (the ten labels, and whom the comment targets) the annotator says, of the comment. What the
# set measured of the comment, and what it holds of the annotator, the set says. The card's feature list does not say
# whom infitms, outfitms, std_err and hypothesis belong to; it lists them in the order hate_speech_score, text,
# infitms, outfitms, annotator_severity, std_err, annotator_infitms, annotator_outfitms, hypothesis, and the recipe
# records the four of the comment.
# A comment is its text; comment_id is its pointer. The annotator ID is content
# beside each judgment, and the corpus trunk is the sole witness.
match train-*.tsv

tier row by \n
header
escaped \
tier field by \t

thing row text
key row comment_id
content annotator_id
content text platform hate_speech_score infitms outfitms std_err hypothesis sentiment respect insult humiliate status dehumanize violence genocide attack_defend hatespeech target_* annotator_*

# The card: "hate_speech_score - continuous hate speech measure"
relation "continuous hate speech measure" hate_speech_score
# Kennedy et al. (2020), the card's paper: "Social media comments were collected from three popular platforms:
# YouTube, Reddit, and Twitter."
relation "Social media comments were collected from" platform
# Kennedy et al. (2020): "We used the identity relevance and hate speech hypothesis scores to create five
# stratification bins"
relation "hate speech hypothesis scores" hypothesis
# Sachdeva et al. (2022), the card's other paper: "an infit mean-squared statistic, a rater fit diagnostic"
relation "infit mean-squared statistic" infitms annotator_infitms
# The card: "annotator_severity - annotator's estimated survey interpretation bias"
relation "annotator's estimated survey interpretation bias" annotator_severity
# The ten survey items, in the prompts Sachdeva et al. (2022) give them ("Table 1: Survey items and ordinal responses
# given to annotators for each comment"):
#   Sentiment "How would you describe the sentiment of this comment?"
#   Respect "Is this comment respectful towards the group(s) you previously identified?"
#   Insult "Do you agree or disagree with the following statement: This comment is insulting towards the group(s) you
#   previously identified."
#   Humiliate "... This comment is humiliating towards the group(s) you previously identified."
#   Status "This comment states that the group(s) you previously identified is:"
#   Dehumanize "... This comment dehumanizes the group(s) you previously identified (e.g., by comparing them to an
#   animal)."
#   Violence "... This comment calls for using violence against the group(s) you previously identified."
#   Genocide "... This comment calls for the deliberate killing of a large group of people from the group(s) you
#   previously identified."
#   Attack-Defend "Is the comment attacking or defending the group(s) you previously identified?"
#   Hate speech "Does this comment contain hate speech, defined as ..."
# (the engine keeps a relation's words to 63 bytes, so each is the prompt's statement up to the group)
relation "How would you describe the sentiment of this comment?" sentiment
relation "Is this comment respectful towards the group(s)" respect
relation "This comment is insulting towards the group(s)" insult
relation "This comment is humiliating towards the group(s)" humiliate
relation "This comment states that the group(s)" status
relation "This comment dehumanizes the group(s)" dehumanize
relation "This comment calls for using violence against the group(s)" violence
relation "calls for the deliberate killing of a large group of people" genocide
relation "Is the comment attacking or defending the group(s)" attack_defend
relation "Does this comment contain hate speech" hatespeech
# The binary target checklist and voluntary demographics are documented in
# Sachdeva et al. (2022), sections 4.3-4.4 and Appendix B:
# https://aclanthology.org/2022.nlperspectives-1.11.pdf
# Every checkbox remains a boolean answer, including false; it is not an
# unconditional identity assertion. Other/refused choices retain their group.
# Rater outfit is identified by the dataset author as a rater fit diagnostic:
# https://huggingface.co/datasets/ucberkeley-dlab/measuring-hate-speech/discussions/3
# Kennedy et al. (2020), section 4.2, calls outfit the outlier-sensitive mean square:
# https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.10277v1
relation "outlier-sensitive mean-squared fit statistic" outfitms annotator_outfitms
# std_err is still an unresolved obligation: its quantity is not documented.
attest row platform hate_speech_score infitms outfitms std_err hypothesis
attest row sentiment respect insult humiliate status dehumanize violence genocide attack_defend hatespeech target_* with annotator_id
# The annotator columns are named one by one: annotator_id, the annotator itself, is not said of itself.
attest row annotator_severity annotator_infitms annotator_outfitms annotator_gender annotator_trans annotator_educ annotator_income annotator_ideology annotator_age annotator_gender_* annotator_transgender* annotator_cisgender annotator_education_* annotator_income_* annotator_ideology_* annotator_race_* annotator_religion_* annotator_sexuality_* of annotator_id

# Whether the comment is directed at or about the named identity group.
relation "directed at or about individuals based on race or ethnicity" target_race
relation "directed at or about individuals: Asian" target_race_asian
relation "directed at or about individuals: Black or African American" target_race_black
relation "directed at or about individuals: Latino or non-white Hispanic" target_race_latinx
relation "directed at or about individuals: Middle Eastern" target_race_middle_eastern
relation "directed at or about individuals: Native American or Alaska Native" target_race_native_american
relation "directed at or about individuals: Pacific Islander" target_race_pacific_islander
relation "directed at or about individuals: non-Hispanic White" target_race_white
relation "directed at or about individuals: other racial or ethnic identity" target_race_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on religious affiliation" target_religion
relation "directed at or about individuals: atheist" target_religion_atheist
relation "directed at or about individuals: Buddhist" target_religion_buddhist
relation "directed at or about individuals: Christian" target_religion_christian
relation "directed at or about individuals: Hindu" target_religion_hindu
relation "directed at or about individuals: Jewish" target_religion_jewish
relation "directed at or about individuals: Mormon" target_religion_mormon
relation "directed at or about individuals: Muslim" target_religion_muslim
relation "directed at or about individuals: other religious affiliation" target_religion_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on national origin or citizenship status" target_origin
relation "directed at or about individuals: immigrants" target_origin_immigrant
relation "directed at or about individuals: migrant workers" target_origin_migrant_worker
relation "directed at or about individuals: people from a specific country" target_origin_specific_country
relation "directed at or about individuals: undocumented people" target_origin_undocumented
relation "directed at or about individuals: other national origin or citizenship status" target_origin_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on gender identity" target_gender
relation "directed at or about individuals: men" target_gender_men
relation "directed at or about individuals: women" target_gender_women
relation "directed at or about individuals: non-binary or third gender" target_gender_non_binary
relation "directed at or about individuals: transgender men" target_gender_transgender_men
relation "directed at or about individuals: transgender women" target_gender_transgender_women
relation "directed at or about individuals: transgender, unspecified" target_gender_transgender_unspecified
relation "directed at or about individuals: other gender identity" target_gender_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on sexual orientation" target_sexuality
relation "directed at or about individuals: bisexual" target_sexuality_bisexual
relation "directed at or about individuals: gay" target_sexuality_gay
relation "directed at or about individuals: lesbian" target_sexuality_lesbian
relation "directed at or about individuals: heterosexual" target_sexuality_straight
relation "directed at or about individuals: other sexual orientation" target_sexuality_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on age" target_age
relation "directed at or about individuals: children, ages 0-12" target_age_children
relation "directed at or about individuals: teenagers, ages 13-17" target_age_teenagers
relation "directed at or about individuals: young adults, ages 18-39" target_age_young_adults
relation "directed at or about individuals: middle-aged adults, ages 40-64" target_age_middle_aged
relation "directed at or about individuals: seniors, ages 65 and older" target_age_seniors
relation "directed at or about individuals: other age group" target_age_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on disability status" target_disability
relation "directed at or about individuals: physical disability" target_disability_physical
relation "directed at or about individuals: cognitive or learning disability" target_disability_cognitive
relation "directed at or about individuals: neurological disability" target_disability_neurological
relation "directed at or about individuals: visual impairment" target_disability_visually_impaired
relation "directed at or about individuals: hearing impairment" target_disability_hearing_impaired
relation "directed at or about individuals: unspecified disability" target_disability_unspecific
relation "directed at or about individuals: other disability" target_disability_other
relation "directed at or about individuals based on political identity" target_politics
relation "directed at or about individuals: alt-right" target_politics_alt_right
relation "directed at or about individuals: communist" target_politics_communist
relation "directed at or about individuals: conservative" target_politics_conservative
relation "directed at or about individuals: Democrat" target_politics_democrat
relation "directed at or about individuals: Green Party" target_politics_green_party
relation "directed at or about individuals: leftist" target_politics_leftist
relation "directed at or about individuals: liberal" target_politics_liberal
relation "directed at or about individuals: libertarian" target_politics_libertarian
relation "directed at or about individuals: Republican" target_politics_republican
relation "directed at or about individuals: socialist" target_politics_socialist
relation "directed at or about individuals: other political identity" target_politics_other

# Voluntary answers about the annotator, never the comment.
relation "self-reported gender identity" annotator_gender
relation "self-reported transgender identification" annotator_trans
relation "self-reported educational level" annotator_educ
relation "self-reported income" annotator_income
relation "self-reported political affiliation" annotator_ideology
relation "self-reported age" annotator_age
relation "self-reported gender choice selected: men" annotator_gender_men
relation "self-reported gender choice selected: women" annotator_gender_women
relation "self-reported gender choice selected: non-binary or third gender" annotator_gender_non_binary
relation "self-reported gender choice selected: prefers not to state gender" annotator_gender_prefer_not_to_say
relation "self-reported gender choice selected: self-described gender" annotator_gender_self_describe
relation "self-reported education choice selected: some high school" annotator_education_some_high_school
relation "self-reported education choice selected: completed high school" annotator_education_high_school_grad
relation "self-reported education choice selected: some college" annotator_education_some_college
relation "self-reported education choice selected: associate degree" annotator_education_college_grad_aa
relation "self-reported education choice selected: bachelor's degree" annotator_education_college_grad_ba
relation "self-reported education choice selected: professional degree" annotator_education_professional_degree
relation "self-reported education choice selected: master's degree" annotator_education_masters
relation "self-reported education choice selected: doctorate" annotator_education_phd
relation "self-reported income choice selected: below $10,000" annotator_income_<10k
relation "self-reported income choice selected: $10,000-$50,000" annotator_income_10k-50k
relation "self-reported income choice selected: $50,000-$100,000" annotator_income_50k-100k
relation "self-reported income choice selected: $100,000-$200,000" annotator_income_100k-200k
relation "self-reported income choice selected: above $200,000" annotator_income_>200k
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: extremely conservative" annotator_ideology_extremeley_conservative
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: conservative" annotator_ideology_conservative
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: slightly conservative" annotator_ideology_slightly_conservative
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: neutral" annotator_ideology_neutral
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: slightly liberal" annotator_ideology_slightly_liberal
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: liberal" annotator_ideology_liberal
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: extremely liberal" annotator_ideology_extremeley_liberal
relation "self-reported ideology choice selected: no political opinion" annotator_ideology_no_opinion
relation "self-reported race choice selected: Asian" annotator_race_asian
relation "self-reported race choice selected: Black or African American" annotator_race_black
relation "self-reported race choice selected: Latino or non-white Hispanic" annotator_race_latinx
relation "self-reported race choice selected: Middle Eastern" annotator_race_middle_eastern
relation "self-reported race choice selected: Native American or Alaska Native" annotator_race_native_american
relation "self-reported race choice selected: Pacific Islander" annotator_race_pacific_islander
relation "self-reported race choice selected: non-Hispanic White" annotator_race_white
relation "self-reported race choice selected: other racial or ethnic identity" annotator_race_other
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: atheist" annotator_religion_atheist
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: Buddhist" annotator_religion_buddhist
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: Christian" annotator_religion_christian
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: Hindu" annotator_religion_hindu
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: Jewish" annotator_religion_jewish
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: Mormon" annotator_religion_mormon
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: Muslim" annotator_religion_muslim
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: other religious affiliation" annotator_religion_other
relation "self-reported religion choice selected: no religious affiliation" annotator_religion_nothing
relation "self-reported sexuality choice selected: bisexual" annotator_sexuality_bisexual
relation "self-reported sexuality choice selected: gay" annotator_sexuality_gay
relation "self-reported sexuality choice selected: heterosexual" annotator_sexuality_straight
relation "self-reported sexuality choice selected: other sexual orientation" annotator_sexuality_other
relation "self-reported transgender choice selected" annotator_transgender
relation "self-reported cisgender choice selected" annotator_cisgender
relation "prefers not to state transgender identification" annotator_transgender_prefer_not_to_say
